From 8a529f53fabd2186d673cdcf1bf834a5edba5227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan <dev.in@gnu6.live>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:13:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(residency): expert residency for Qwen3-Next and
 qwen35moe GGUF

The residency runtime setup moves from qwen3_moe into
moe::runtime_from_environment, shared by Qwen3 MoE and Qwen3-Next (the model
qwen35moe GGUFs load through). SparseMoeBlock builds its routed experts with
MoEExperts::new_resident when residency is requested; the shared expert and
its gate are unchanged. The normal pipeline's gate accepts
Qwen3NextForCausalLM, and Qwen3NextLoader drops the routed stacks from the
mapped layer sizes under residency, as Qwen3MoELoader does since 0007.

Qwen3 MoE behaviour is unchanged: residency captures are byte-identical to
the 0010 build on the synthetic qwen3moe fixture.

